# sprint.md command registry — THE source of truth for the command catalog.
#
# Every user-facing command has exactly one row here. The runtime index
# (./sprint.sh help) is GENERATED from this file, and ./sprint.sh validate
# --commands enforces that the dispatch table, the help/*.md pages, and
# DOCUMENTATION.md all match it. Add a command = add a row here + a help page;
# the index updates itself and the validator guards the rest.
#
# Format (pipe-delimited, 4 fields):
#   command | group | usage-suffix | one-line summary
# group is one of: create | chat | plan | work | look | keep
# usage-suffix is the arg hint shown after the command (may be empty).
# Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored. Order within a group is
# display order. A command may have a second row for a notable sub-form
# (e.g. validate --docs); existence checks dedupe on the command field.

newidea       | create   | [name]              | Create a new idea (no name = AI Q&A)
newfeature    | create   | [name]              | Create a new feature (no name = AI Q&A)
newtask       | create   | <description>       | Create a new task
newplan       | create   | <name> [task-id...] | Create a plan — a named list of task IDs grouping related work
newbug        | create   | <description>       | Report a new bug
newtest       | create   | <name>              | Create a test loop to validate a deployed thing

chat          | chat     | [target]            | id: define/refine/split one task · folder (blocked/next/backlog): sweep · plan [id]: author a plan · bugs: sweep inbox · nothing: walk sprint health (spine: chat → plan start → work)

plan          | plan     | think/start/done [id] | think: dual-persona plan critique · start: gate + commit members to next/ (the sprint), latches STARTED · done: delete the plan once every member is in done/ — heads the spine → work

work          | work     | [limit] [--fast]    | Execute — happy path: run READY tasks in next/ → review/ (after plan start)
loop          | work     | [--refill] [--retry]| Autopilot spine — plan start refill (gates as it commits) then work drain
gate          | work     | [folder] [limit]    | Off-spine quality gate — re-gate next/ (--force) or report on backlog/doing/blocked (not the happy path)
split         | work     | <path>              | Off-spine — one-shot split of a large task into subtasks (no conversation)
polish        | work     | [limit/file] [--code] [--rounds N] | After work — quality sweep review/, deep-judge a file, or --code audit

status        | look     |                     | Show project status
search        | look     | <keyword>           | Search tasks by keyword
align         | look     |                     | Analyze feature alignment
context       | look     |                     | Generate AI context summary

profile       | keep     |                     | Create or update project profile (interactive)
profile       | keep     | show                | Print current project profile (no AI)
sync          | keep     | [--all]             | Push task changes to GitHub
validate      | keep     | [--fix] [--dry-run] | Integrity-check task IDs and Depends on / Blocks
validate      | keep     | --docs              | Check help/*.md for flag drift vs scripts
validate      | keep     | --commands          | Check every command is fully surfaced (this registry ↔ dispatch ↔ help ↔ manual)
cleanup       | keep     | [--delete/--force/--all] | Clean stale scratch files
deps          | keep     |                     | File a backlog task auditing outdated/vulnerable deps
